        "metadata": {
          "category": "stories",
          "minAge": 3,
          "maxAge": 7,
          "media": {
            "duration": 2315,
            "fileSize": 37433514
          },
          "abridged": false,
          "author": "Maria Isabel Sanchez Vegara,Lisbeth Kaiser",
          "description": "Inspire little ones to follow their dreams with simple, engaging stories about the most impactful women, to listen to at home or on the go. With determination and unique ideas, these bold and talented women changed the world forever. Their journeys from young children to celebrated figures are now available in audio format, including:  \n\nJane Austen, the groundbreaking novelist who portrayed women bravely making their own choices. Malala Yousafzai, the youngest person ever to win a Nobel Peace Prize. Vivienne Westwood, the designer who revolutionized the fashion world. Beyoncé, the superstar singer with most Grammy-nominations in history. Queen Elizabeth, the longest-reigning monarch of modern times. Emmeline Pankhurst, the activist who championed the right of women to vote.  \n\nLittle People, BIG DREAMS is a bestselling biography series for kids that explores the lives of outstanding people, from designers and artists to scientists and activists. All of them achieved incredible things, yet each began life as a child with a dream. This empowering series offers inspiring messages to children of all ages, in a range of formats.  \n\nThis audiobook is ideal for any young girl curious about women’s accomplishments or simply just learning about their favourite celebrity. Listen at home or learn something new in the car or on holiday. An uplifting tape that will be replayed again and again. Inspire the next generation of outstanding people who will change the world with Little People, BIG DREAMS!",
          "note": "US version",
